WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.710
- Learning is so central to
everything human beings do.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.860
Knowledge needs to be absorbed
by people who need it.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.500
Knowledge is a great enabler.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.350
This is what we are.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.710
The mission of Open Learning
is to share knowledge.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.440
We want to make sure that learning
isn't this thing we keep,

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.470
but people can take and
do something with it

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:18.820
for their lives, for their enjoyment,

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.110
for the fulfillment of their
ambitions, their dreams.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.770
So we work with MIT faculty

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.926
and we bring content to the world.

00:00:24.926 --> 00:00:27.310
We are doing research on the science

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:28.980
of learning about how to actually teach,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.160
regardless of whether
you're online or in person.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.450
How do memories form?

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:33.650
How do neurons work?

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.620
How does context impact our learning?

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.790
What we have is a very,
very rich community,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.050
rich in terms of talent,

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.740
rich in terms of diversity of thought,

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.960
diversity of background,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.210
diversity of purpose,
that's a glorious thing.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.420
Open Learning's values have a
lot to do with the word open.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.700
We have to open education.
we have to open learning.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.320
MIT's vision is that
learning has to be free

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.210
and liberated in the sense
that anyone can access it.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.400
It's got to be efficient
so people can access it

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.950
in a way that's most effective.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.910
Some of those things you
can do better online.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:05.900
And some things like coaching or mentoring

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.300
you can do better in person.

00:01:08.302 --> 00:01:11.820
The pandemic has taught us
that the half-life of knowledge

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.960
is even shorter than it was before.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:16.670
Jobs are changing, media has changed.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.620
Entire industries have changed.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.720
That means that human beings

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.260
are going to have to transform themselves.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.560
And the oxygen for that is learning.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.240
There's so much we don't know
and so much we can do better.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.400
So I think this is the beginning
of an incredible journey.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.067
(gentle music)

